  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The requested spatial correlation and RMSE against WOA23 on the 1° grid require putting fields on one grid and using a single common valid-data mask so scores are computed over the same cells.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "For the model–WOA23 map metrics (spatial Pearson correlation, RMSE), regrid each model nitracline map to the WOA23 1° grid, then build one shared valid-data mask over WOA23 and all three regridded models with `build_comparison_mask` and apply it with `.where(mask)` before any metric; report the mask cell counts alongside the metrics.",
        "Use the shared mask only for the cell-by-cell map metrics/ranking; for global and basin mean nitracline depths, compute each source on its own grid/domain, and report model–WOA23 differences as differences of those means, not as a bias on the shared mask."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The question asks for Pacific, Atlantic, and Indian basin means while excluding Southern and Arctic and folding marginal seas into parent oceans, so the basin-partition caveat directly affects how basin statistics must be defined and stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin means must use the WOA23 basin mask on each grid (`select_basin`, `load_basin_mask`), with `include_marginal_seas=True`; state that this WOA23 mask was used and that Pacific/Atlantic/Indian exclude the Southern and Arctic Oceans.",
        "Use the surface basin labels through the full water column (`depth_dependent=False`) for named-ocean basin means of nitracline depth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "The models are on their own native grids with their own areacello, so means should be computed natively for conservation/weighting and regridding used only for maps and pattern comparisons with WOA23.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute every mean depth on each source's own grid with its own weights; regrid to the WOA 1° grid only for the map comparison metrics and Figure 1.",
        "Nitracline depth is a vertical-extremum diagnostic and is quantised by the vertical grid; interpret/model-rank with that caveat stated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "Nitrate units matter for computing the vertical gradient and for sharing one colour scale in Figure 2 because CMIP6 no3 is per unit volume whereas observational products are commonly per unit mass with different scale factors.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`no3` in CMIP6 is `mol m-3` (often reported as `mmol m-3`), while WOA23 nitrate is on a per-mass basis; convert one basis to the other before plotting/model-vs-WOA concentration sections or taking vertical gradients for nitracline depth. The required conversion is `µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ`, using in-situ density if converting below the surface.",
        "The equatorial Pacific section panels must be on one shared concentration unit after this conversion; state which density was used if CMIP6 `no3` was converted (`attrs['density_assumption']`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The three model outputs do not all have the same kind of CMIP6 grid label, notably GFDL-ESM4 being provider-regridded gr while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are native gn, which affects masks and exactness of native-grid operations.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 `no3` is already on `grid_label = gr`, a provider-regridded 1×1 degree archive grid; treat its \"native-grid\" basin/global means as means on that archive grid, and note this when stating methods."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "areacello is the tracer-cell horizontal area needed for the requested global and basin mean nitracline depths on each model grid before any regridding.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Weight native-grid means with each source's own `areacello`; on curvilinear grids the model's own `areacello` is the correct area weight."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested global and basin mean nitracline depths should be area-weighted surface means over ocean cells rather than unweighted averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Global and basin mean nitracline depths are horizontal physical averages, so use area-weighted means (`compute_basic_stat` with `op='area_weighted_mean'`), not plain `mean()`.",
        "Spatial Pearson correlation between nitracline maps should use area weighting (`analyze_correlation` with `weighting='area'`); `compute_difference_metrics` area-weights RMSE by default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "Reading model grids and areacello safely matters because CMIP6 land and below-bottom cells use large missing values that can silently contaminate gradients, masks, and weighted means if CF masking is bypassed.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build the valid mask from each nitracline field itself and use NaN-aware reductions; mask the weights to the same valid cells so land/missing cells stay out of denominators.",
        "For the WOA23 comparison/grid metrics, apply the WOA23 `landsea_01` ocean test as given (`ocean is value > 1`) when defining valid WOA23 ocean cells on the 1° grid."
      ]
    }
